{"questions":[{"question_id":"hT0SedF1Y7T5QFlO","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 1 Offline","year":2011,"examDate":2011,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"gaseous-state","chapterGroup":"physical-chemistry","topic":"kinetic-theory-of-gases","type":"mcqm","marks":2,"negMarks":0.5,"permalink":"according-to-kinetic-theory-of-gases-2011-marks-2-ht0sedf1y7t5qflo.htm","content":"According to kinetic theory of gases","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"collisions are always elastic"},{"identifier":"B","content":"heavier molecules transfer more momentum to the wall of the container"},{"identifier":"C","content":"only a small number molecules have very high velocity"},{"identifier":"D","content":"between collisions, the molecules move in straight line with constant velocity"}],"correct_options":["A","C","D"],"explanation":"<p>(A) When gas molecules collide with each other, high energy molecule transfers some of its energy to less energetic molecule, but the total energy remains conserved. This type of collision between gas molecules is called elastic collision. According to kinetic theory of gas, no loss of energy is observed on collisions and kinetic energy is proportional to absolute temperature of gas.</p>\n<p>Option (A) is correct.</p>\n<p>(B) Momentum of any particle for example, gas molecules depends upon the mass as well as the velocity of the gas. But when there is huge increase in the mass of the gas, its velocity decreases considerably. Hence, heavier gas molecules collides the walls of container with less impact. The transfer of momentum to the walls is very less.</p>\n<p>Option (B) is incorrect.</p>\n<p>(C) Maximum number (no.) of gas molecules have speed distributed around the most probable speed ( <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.65ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.137ex\" height=\"1.652ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -443 1828.8 730.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D463\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D463\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(518,-150) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"6D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6D\"></use><use data-c=\"70\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-70\" transform=\"translate(833,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"73\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-73\" transform=\"translate(1389,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> ). This speed corresponds to the maximum peak of Maxwell-Boltzmann distribution curve.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m03wblkt/99cb1cbd-d1a1-4cc3-afc8-2dbe27a1e4a9/283faad0-5fc2-11ef-9c8f-2bd8696d9aab/file-jaoe38c1m03wblku.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/jaoe38c1m03wblkt/99cb1cbd-d1a1-4cc3-afc8-2dbe27a1e4a9/283faad0-5fc2-11ef-9c8f-2bd8696d9aab/file-jaoe38c1m03wblku.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;max-height:40vh;vertical-align:baseline\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Gaseous State Question 27 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/jaoe38c1m03wblkt/99cb1cbd-d1a1-4cc3-afc8-2dbe27a1e4a9/283faad0-5fc2-11ef-9c8f-2bd8696d9aab/file-jaoe38c1m03wblku.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/jaoe38c1m03wblkt/99cb1cbd-d1a1-4cc3-afc8-2dbe27a1e4a9/283faad0-5fc2-11ef-9c8f-2bd8696d9aab/file-jaoe38c1m03wblku.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m03wblkt/99cb1cbd-d1a1-4cc3-afc8-2dbe27a1e4a9/283faad0-5fc2-11ef-9c8f-2bd8696d9aab/file-jaoe38c1m03wblku.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/jaoe38c1m03wblkt/99cb1cbd-d1a1-4cc3-afc8-2dbe27a1e4a9/283faad0-5fc2-11ef-9c8f-2bd8696d9aab/file-jaoe38c1m03wblku.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/jaoe38c1m03wblkt/99cb1cbd-d1a1-4cc3-afc8-2dbe27a1e4a9/283faad0-5fc2-11ef-9c8f-2bd8696d9aab/file-jaoe38c1m03wblku.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/jaoe38c1m03wblkt/99cb1cbd-d1a1-4cc3-afc8-2dbe27a1e4a9/283faad0-5fc2-11ef-9c8f-2bd8696d9aab/file-jaoe38c1m03wblku.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>There are few molecules which have very high speed (the shaded area under the curve). \n<br><br>Option <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.566ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.394ex\" height=\"2.262ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 1500 1000\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"28\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-28\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(389,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"43\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-43\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1111,0)\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-29\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> is correct.</p>\n\n(D) Molecules are assumed to be moving in straight line with constant velocities. \n<br><br>Option (D) is correct."}]}